==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Etymology===
From {{der|nb|non|þorp}}, from {{der|nb|gem-pro|*þurpą}}, whence also {{cog|de|Dorf}}, {{cog|nds-de|Dörp}}, {{m|nds-de|Dorp}}, {{m|nds-de|Daarp}} and {{cog|nl|dorp}}.

===Noun===
{{nb-noun-n1}}

# {{q|most common}} A solitary [[farm]], distant from other [[settlement]]s.
# {{q|optional}} A solitary group of farms, distant from other settlements.
# {{q|optional before 1960s}} A solitary farm without owned [[land]], renting land from a larger farm nearby.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|nb|torper}}

===See also===
* {{l|nb|husmannsplass}}
* {{l|nb|småbruk}}

